THIRD-PARTY EXCEPTIONS (these are NOT covered by the licence above)
------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Datasets.  The object-detection corpora used in the paper (AI-TOD, DOTA v1
   and v1.5, DIOR, the Mendeley face-mask records, D-Fire, SHWD, xView and the
   COCO 2017 validation set) are third-party works.  They are NOT redistributed
   here, they are NOT covered by the CC BY 4.0 grant above, and each remains
   under its own terms and its own citation requirement.  Where a corpus is
   named only by a public download pointer in the manuscript, that pointer is
   the authoritative source; the archive that produced the paper holds no copy
   of six of the seven corpora, as section 10 defect 6 of the article states.
   At least one of the sources used for the detection datasets is restricted to
   academic use; check the source before any reuse.

2. Third-party training logs.  The twenty public training logs (six sources)
   analysed in section 5.5 are not redistributed.  Only their hashes and source
   pointers are given, because five of those sources state no licence at all.

3. Software and pinned repositories.  The detector frameworks (Ultralytics
   YOLO, YOLOX, Detectron2, MMDetection, DETR, PaddleDetection) and the
   benchmark releases are cited, not vendored; their licences apply to them.

No warranty of any kind is given for any file in this repository.
